        "surveyID": "108481",
        "narrative": "<p>Fish populations are dominated by cisco, followed by walleye, northern pike, and smallmouth bass. A few white sucker, rock bass, and largemouth bass were also captured. Size of cisco, northern pike, sucker and walleye are all larger than average for the area. Some very large walleye (over 22 17 despite an apparent year class failure in 1989. Walleye growth is exceptional during the second and third years. After age 4, some individual walleye continue to grow quite fast, while others grow much more slowly. Since the walleye were not sexed, it is uncertain whether this differential growth is due to forage differences (some walleye were eating cisco) or sex differences. </p>",
