        "surveyID": "20162425037008001",
        "narrative": "<p>Disappointment is an 894-acre lake located 22 miles northeast of Ely in the Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness. It is comparable to nearby Moose and Ensign lakes. The lake is clear and has predominantly rocky shorelines with some areas of sand and muck. The southern portion of the lake is generally shallower and has areas of abundant vegetation, while the northern portion is deeper and steeper.  Disappointment was thermally stratified during a targeted survey on 07/29/24 with dissolved oxygen fading below levels suitable for fish at 16 feet.  <br> \n <br> \nDisappointment is accessed through either a 140-rod portage from Snowbank Lake or a 90-rod portage from Parent Lake. Twelve USFS-maintained campsites are present, and during peak season they can be difficult to come by. The lake is along major canoe routes and campers should expect to see a fair bit of paddle traffic. A 20-rod portage connects to Ahsub lake and canoe routes farther east. <br> \n <br> \nThe total catch of 12.2 fish/net was lower than in previous surveys. The fish population was dominated almost entirely by walleye, followed by northern pike, and smallmouth bass. Low numbers of white sucker, rock bass, and cisco were also present. Yellow perch were conspicuously absent from the survey catch, but present in walleye stomachs.  <br> \n <br> \nWalleye catch per unit effort (8.5/net) was higher than typical for Disappointment. Walleye sizes ranged from 10 to 26 inches. Average length was about 16 inches, which is slightly less than in past surveys. Walleye numbers were driven by strong 2020- and 2021-year classes, but recruitment was consistent most years. Growth was a bit faster than average for the area.  <br> \n <br> \nNorthern pike numbers (1.3/net) were low compared to past surveys. Pike sizes ranged from 22 to 37 inches and averaged 27 inches. This was above average for the area but typical for Disappointment. Northen pike greater than 40 inches have been surveyed previously, and a rare silver-phase color morph is present. <br> \n <br> \nCisco abundance (0.5/net) was the lowest sampled to date. Lengths ranged from 9 to 17 inches and averaged 12 inches. Past cisco catches in Disappointment have been quite variable (1.0-31.2/net) and may be influenced by set locations and date more than population dynamics.  <br> \n <br> \nSmallmouth bass numbers (0.8/net) were close to average for Disappointment. Smallmouth sizes ranged from 5 to 18 inches and averaged 12 inches. Gill nets underrepresent bass populations and smallmouth are almost certainly more abundant than this survey may suggest. No largemouth were captured this survey but they have been sampled in low abundance in previous investigations.  <br> \n</p>",
        "surveySubType": "Standard Survey",
