        "surveyDate": "1993-09-07",
        "surveyID": "108508",
        "narrative": "<p>Trap nets were not set on this lake due to inaccessibility.  All fish information is from gill nets.Fish populations in 1993 were dominated by cisco, followed by walleye, northern pike, and smallmouth bass.  Low numbers of white sucker, rock bass, largemouth bass, and yellow perch were also captured.Cisco sizes ranged from 8\" to 18\" and averaged 11.9\".  Some large northern pike (36\") and walleye (over 25\") were present.Recruitment of the major species is good.  Smallmouth bass growth (8.1\" at Annulus V) is slow by area standards.  Growth of northern pike and yellow perch is average.  Walleye growth is average at Annulus II (9.8\"), but is faster than average thereafter (14.7\" at Annulus III; 16.7\" at Annulus IV).Populations of all fish averaged 25.1 fish/gill net (27.8 lbs/gill net).</p>"
